dialogue cohesion_generic_striker_mage
title: Half a breath
trigger: Cohesion role:Striker role:Mage level=4
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker with $with
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  Behind the wagons the Striker is drawing lines in the dirt with a stick, and the Mage is rubbing them out with a boot as fast as they go down.
  -> lines

node lines hero
  Every fight you run into my circle half a breath before it closes. Half a breath. I've held a spell back three times this week for you.
  -> breath

node breath with
  And three times the thing in the circle was still standing because you waited. If I don't go in, it walks out of your circle and onto whoever's behind us.
  -> stick

node stick hero
  Commander, one of us is going to get the other killed. I'd rather it was settled out here, with a stick.
  * Call it out loud. The Mage says the count, the Striker goes on the last word. -> count
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 10
  * The Mage casts on time, every time. The Striker learns the circle. -> circle
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 6
  * Hold back, both of you. I'll call every fight myself. -> hold
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -3

node count with
  A count. Three, two, and I'm gone on one. I can hear a count over anything.
  -> trust

node circle with
  Learn the circle. All right. Draw it for me again, slower, and don't rub it out this time.
  -> trust

node hold hero
  Then we wait on you every time. Fine. But the fights won't.
  -> trust

node trust hero
  The truth is, I've never had anyone fast enough to be in the circle at all. Most people run away from it.
  -> away

node away with
  Running away from a spell is sense. Running into one is trust. You've never once dropped it on me.
  * That's the closest thing to a promise either of you has made. Keep it. -> promise
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 9
  * Trust is good. Practice is better. Again tomorrow, at first light. -> practice
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 7
  * Don't make it sound grander than it is. It's timing. -> timing
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -2

node promise hero
  Then here's mine. I'll never close the circle while you're inside it. Not once.
  -> close

node practice with
  First light. Bring the stick. I'll bring the feet.
  -> close

node timing hero
  Timing, then. Mine's good. Yours is getting there.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Mage draws one more circle in the dirt. This time the Striker stands in the middle of it, grinning, and the Mage counts aloud, slowly, down to one.
